---
import { site } from '../content/site';
import CopyCommand from './CopyCommand.astro';
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden border-t border-white/5 bg-white/[0.02]">
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 hero-glow opacity-60"></div>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 sm:py-20 text-center">
    <h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">
      Two commands. <span class="text-gradient">One project.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-lg text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
      Run init inside one repo. It adds the repo's store and a block in the CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md already there. On
      your machine it adds Claude Code hooks, Codex hooks or the OpenCode plugin if the repo uses them, and a daily
      6:15am run. <a class="link" href="#get-started">Get started</a> lists every change and the flags that skip each one.
    </p>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-9 max-w-lg space-y-3 text-left" data-reveal>
      <CopyCommand command={site.installCmd} size="lg" />
      <CopyCommand command={site.initCmd} size="lg" />
    </div>

    <!-- The scan is a second step, and what it changes comes before its command. -->
    <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-lg text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
      Many repos at once is a second step. This command gives every git repo in your home folder and up to three levels
      below it a store of its own, seeded from a year of its commits, plus the same user-level hooks and daily run. It
      patches no CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md.
    </p>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-lg text-left" data-reveal>
      <CopyCommand command={site.scanCmd} />
    </div>

    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3" data-reveal>
      <a
        href={site.links.repo}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-white/12 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-200 transition hover:bg-white/5"
      >
        Star on GitHub
      </a>
      <a
        href={site.links.npm}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-white/12 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-200 transition hover:bg-white/5"
      >
        View on npm
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
